  "answer": "To declare and validate query parameters in FastAPI, you can use the `Query` function from the `fastapi` module. Here's how you can do it:\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, Query\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.get(\"/items/\")\nasync def read_items(q: str | None = Query(None, max_length=50)):\n    return {\"q\": q}\n```\n\nThis example uses the `Query` function to specify that the `q` parameter is of type `str | None` and has a maximum length of 50 characters. FastAPI will validate the data to ensure it meets this requirement.",
